{"baseRefOid":"c6975ca76f9f667f1250ba403d0e6da2aafe14d0","body":"This PR contains a verified counterexample to Conjecture 7.5 as printed on p.474 of Ohtsuki’s collection. For the full ordinary SU(5) invariant at WZW level 5 (shifted level 10), L(5,1) and L(5,2) both have fundamental group Z/5, but their positive S3-normalized squared magnitudes are 3475 + 1550 sqrt(5) and 4025 + 1800 sqrt(5). The proof uses established modular-category and RT/Hansen–Takata surgery inputs; an analytic A4 root-lattice reduction and exact cyclotomic certificates independently reproduce the calculation.\n\nPublished qualified research note and verification package: [DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23174156](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23174156). Two sequential fresh whole-package adversarial reviews completed, with the first review’s ancestor-link integrity-guard correction propagated into the final package and a new second review finding no required repairs. All seven published files match the reviewed bytes; the Google Sheets tracker has a uniquely verified entry at ‘Math Puzzles’!A28:D28. The final verification package includes optimization-safe guards and actual recorded runs; the incoming proof and historical review evidence are preserved in the audit archive. Repository merge and native acceptance follow publication.\n\nHistorical priority remains unresolved. Takahito Kuriya’s directly relevant preprint, *The LMO invariant and the Guadagnini–Pilo conjecture for lens spaces*, is credited, but its full text could not be obtained. We cannot establish that it does not already contain or circumscribe this result. No first counterexample, exhaustive novelty clearance, current global openness, or new historical resolution is claimed. Other source and edition gaps are disclosed in the public priority supplement. The human specifically authorized publication with this qualification.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting, reproduction, literature comparison and adversarial verification. The preprint is unrefereed and has not undergone conventional human peer review. The original `claimed_solved` status and author effort `2/5` are preserved; there were zero new central proof-search turns. This counterexample concerns full ordinary SU(5), with no claim against the known SU(2) lens-space theorem.\n","headRefOid":"6534ad01e519c719628a18984b108e73cf2e8ead","isDraft":true,"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":95,"state":"OPEN"}
